WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.770
Nothing says summer quite like baseball and
childhood nostalgia, and no film better encompasses

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.000
the two than The Sandlot.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.540
The classic film about baseball and growing
up introduced audiences to a charming group

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.540
of child actors.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.220
What has the cast of this family-friendly
classic been up to?

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.660
The anticipation is killing us, Smalls!

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.880
Tom Guiry was just 11 years old when he was
cast as new kid in town Scotty Smalls, the

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.620
New York native's feature film debut.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.900
Guiry, who started acting to deal with his
shyness, landed an agent after she saw him

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:29.680
in a local play.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.500
The Sandlot was one of his first big auditions,
but he didn't initially get the part.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.300
Luckily for Guiry, the other actor didn't
work out, so he came back to screen test again,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.580
and he knocked it out of the park.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.899
Guiry followed up his work in The Sandlot
with a role in the 1994 family film Lassie,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.409
and yet another baseball film, The Last Home
Run, in 1996.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.920
However, the shy kid eventually blossomed
into an actor who's mostly made a career out

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.960
of playing tough men.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:00.420
He appeared in Mystic River and played a fur
trapper alongside Tom Hardy and Leonardo DiCaprio

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.020
in The Revenant.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.579
Though Mike Vitar made a considerable impression
on young audiences as star player Benny "the

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.860
Jet" Rodriguez, he only made a handful of
appearances in film and TV afterwards.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.240
Following The Sandlot, he continued to display
his athletic abilities on film as Luis Mendoza

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.880
in two Mighty Ducks sequels, but he quit acting
in 1997.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.770
In the midst of his acting career, Vitar started
training in Emergency Medical Services in

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.220
the Los Angeles area, eventually becoming
a firefighter in 2002.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.420
He was honored the following year for his
work saving two fellow firefighters during

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.140
a house fire in the Hollywood Hills.

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:39.700
Unfortunately, not all of Vitar's actions
have been heroic: he was arrested in 2015

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:43.720
after allegedly assaulting a grad student
on Halloween in northwest Los Angeles with

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:44.960
two other firefighters.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.460
Patrick Renna stole bases and hearts as Hamilton
"Ham" Porter with one line:

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.240
"You're killing me, Smalls."

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.270
He reunited with Sandlot castmate Chauncey
Leopardi two years later in the soccer flick

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.360
The Big Green, following a turn opposite comedian
Pauly Shore in Son in Law.

00:02:00.569 --> 00:02:04.560
Renna continued working throughout the '90s,
appearing on plenty of television favorites

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.600
like Home Improvement, Boy Meets World, The
X-Files and a string of movies.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:14.060
More recently, he appeared in the Kickstarter-funded
film Bad Roomies, which he also co-produced.

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:18.370
Renna also recently returned to the screen
in a big way with a recurring guest role in

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:22.580
the Netflix wrestling dramedy GLOW as the
socially awkward superfan, Cupcake.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:28.180
Chauncey Leopardi made his film debut in 1991's
Father of the Bride remake starring Steve

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:28.680
Martin.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.280
Just 12 years old on the set of The Sandlot,
Leopardi admitted that he would constantly

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.900
pester director David Mickey Evans about when
they'd be filming his character's kiss with

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.580
lifeguard Wendy Peffercorn.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:42.840
"What?"

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.640
Leopardi worked quite a bit after receiving
his poolside CPR, popping up in '90s faves

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.980
like Casper with Christina Ricci, who he co-starred
with again in The Opposite of Sex in 1998.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.470
He also played bully Alan on the beloved cult
TV show Freaks and Geeks.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.180
"Bill, you want some crushed nuts with your
Sunday?"

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.240
"My what?"

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:05.740
"Ah"

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:06.740
"Hahaha"

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.260
Leopardi also had a recurring role on Gilmore
Girls.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:17.000
From 2009-2012, Leopardi made a living as
a professional poker player, but a big loss

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.260
forced him into the job market.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.840
He lives in Los Angeles with his daughter,
and regularly appears at special fan events

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:23.640
and screenings.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:25.840
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.689
Like more than one of his Sandlot castmates,
Marty York made his screen debut in the film,

00:03:30.689 --> 00:03:34.849
which he followed with small parts on Saved
by the Bell: the College Years and a couple

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:35.760
of episodes of Boy Meets World.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:42.140
Other than Sandlot fan events and a 2015 episode
of Adult Swim's The Eric Andre Show, the place

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:47.269
he's appeared the most has been gossip site
TMZ, which reported he was arrested for alleged

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:49.300
domestic violence in 2009.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:54.780
Since his "little league days," York has transformed
from scrawny kid to buff personal trainer,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.069
and at one point he was working on developing
a line of workout supplements he dubbed "Beast

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:04.019
Juice", a reference Sandlot fans will recognize
as being inspired by the fearsome dog the

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:04.980
crew has to face.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.760
Brandon Quintin Adams was one of the few kids
in the cast who already had quite a bit of

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.300
acting experience prior to appearing in The
Sandlot.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:17.940
Adams got his start dancing in Michael Jackson's
1988 music video for "Smooth Criminal."

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.440
He did quite a bit of TV in the late '80s,
and made his feature film debut in Wes Craven's

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.260
1991 horror flick The People Under the Stairs.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.790
After the success of The Sandlot, he appeared
again alongside castmate Karen Allen in Ghost

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:35.120
in the Machine and reunited with Mike Vitar
in D2: the Mighty Ducks.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.160
After doing some voiceover work for the video
game Kingdom Hearts II in the late 2000s,

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.260
Adams pivoted into a hip-hop career, releasing
an album called B Lee H.D.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:50.280
Grant Gelt got his start with a string of
TV appearances on Knots Landing, Tales from

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:54.940
the Crypt, Northern Exposure and others, making
his film debut in the Steven Seagal action

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.980
movie Marked for Death in 1991.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.860
However, The Sandlot gave him the biggest
role of his short acting career.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:05.320
Gelt has since started a new chapter in his
career, moving from artist management into

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:10.040
a senior executive role at the artist-to-fan
engagement platform Fullscreen Direct.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.660
Actor Shane Obedzinski's on-screen career
was brief.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:19.040
He made his feature film debut in 1991's My
Girl, starring Macaulay Culkin, and was cast

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.940
as little Tommy "Repeat" in The Sandlot a
couple of years later after an audition in

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:23.480
Orlando.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.520
Obedzinski quit acting after The Sandlot and
returned to Florida to finish school.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:32.680
After graduating, he toured for a few years
with a local band before opening his own pizza

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.100
parlor in Brandon, Florida.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:39.060
Denis Leary was still relatively new to acting
when he appeared in The Sandlot as Scotty

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.420
Smalls' stepfather Bill.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.700
He'd spent nearly a decade working his way
up the stand-up comedy circuit in Boston and

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.740
New York before his one-man show No Cure For
Cancer catapulted him to fame.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:53.620
Leary continued making a name for himself
throughout the '90s in everything from Demolition

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.400
Man to Pixar's A Bug's Life.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:59.880
He was a regular on the late-night circuit
and continued performing stand-up, as well

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.550
as producing Comics Come Home, the annual
TV special for charity featuring prominent

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.120
comedians.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:10.330
Leary is perhaps best known for his Emmy-nominated
performance and writing on the FX firefighter

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:12.920
dramedy Rescue Me, which ran for seven seasons.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:17.800
He also wrote, produced, and starred in the
series Sax&amp;Hugs&amp;Rock&amp;Roll for FX.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:22.400
But he's still had plenty of other career
home runs thanks in the HBO drama Recount

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.900
and appearances in two Amazing Spider-Man
films

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.340
"I was wrong about you Peter.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.260
This city needs you.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.180
You're gonna need this."

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:39.700
He may not have been able to handle a certain
treehouse vacuum cleaner, but Victor DiMattia

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.220
certainly cleaned up when it came to booking
acting jobs.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:47.740
Prior to playing Timmy Timmons, DiMattia appeared
on TV as Dennis the Menace, as well as TV

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.920
shows like Family Ties, and Punky Brewster.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:54.820
He made his big-screen debut in Turner &amp; Hooch
with Tom Hanks and worked with rapper Vanilla

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.760
Ice on his ill-fated screen debut, Cool As
Ice.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:02.480
DiMattia quit acting a few years after The
Sandlot and pursued other interests, including

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.320
playing in a band.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:08.580
He works as a bartender in L.A., writes comedy,
and hangs out on occasion with castmate Marty

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.620
York, in addition to putting in regular appearances
at Sandlot fan events.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:18.280
On top of that, he also runs a pop culture-centered
podcast called Vic in a Box, which he launched

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:22.640
in mid-2017 with a commentary segment on being
part of The Sandlot.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:28.060
The Sandlot cemented Marley Shelton's place
as an all-time movie dreamgirl the minute

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:33.180
she appeared onscreen in Wendy Peffercorn's
signature red bathing suit and white sunglasses.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.090
Up until that point, Shelton had mostly TV
credits on her résumé, but after The Sandlot,

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.400
her career really took off.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:44.330
The California blonde later appeared in Pleasantville
and Never Been Kissed and wasn't afraid to

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.900
go grindhouse for Quentin Tarantino in 2007's
Death Proof.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:53.360
She appeared in the stylish Sin City and has
worked with Oliver Stone twice: in 1995's

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:59.620
Nixon and 2008's W. She also popped up as
Joan's BFF on an episode of Mad Men in 2013.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:04.420
Most recently, she appeared alongside Dwayne
"The Rock" Johnson in his 2018 video game

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.720
adaptation Rampage.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.500
Veteran character actor Art LaFleur had some
pretty legendary cleats to fill when he accepted

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.080
the role of The Babe in The Sandlot.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:18.500
Luckily, LaFleur already had a couple of baseball
films under his belt, Mr. Baseball and Field

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.840
of Dreams, making him something of a sports
film MVP.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:26.700
He's worked fairly consistently ever since,
appearing in cult classics like The Blob,

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:30.670
family fare like The Santa Clause 2, and episodes
of House and Key and Peele.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:36.000
By the time Karen Allen appeared as the empathetic
mom in The Sandlot, she'd already cemented

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:42.279
her place in fans' hearts as Katy in 1978's
classic frat comedy Animal House and Indiana

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:46.140
Jones' gal pal Marion Ravenwood in 1981's
Raiders of the Lost Ark.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:47.900
"Indiana Jones.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.800
I always knew someday you'd come walkin back
through my door."

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:00.500
Spunky and likable, Allen made for an affable
sparring partner to Bill Murray in Scrooged,

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:05.320
and turned on the waterworks in John Carpenter's
sci-fi drama Starman opposite Jeff Bridges.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:10.640
After her son was born in 1990, Allen took
smaller roles, such as her work in The Sandlot,

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:12.320
so she could spend more time with her family.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.460
In 1993, she and her son moved to Massachusetts
into a converted barn she'd purchased.

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:21.829
She got involved in the local theatre scene,
acting in and directing plays at the Berkshire

00:09:21.829 --> 00:09:24.200
Theatre Festival and teaching classes.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:28.660
Steven Spielberg managed to lure her back
for the fourth Indy flick, Indiana Jones and

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:33.250
the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull in 2008,
but Allen has mostly remained happily out

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:33.920
of the spotlight.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:38.800
Like his character in The Sandlot, James Earl
Jones has his own history with baseball, at

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.600
least onscreen and in the theatre.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:46.399
Prior to appearing as the reclusive Mr. Mertle
in the 1993 flick, Jones similarly opined

00:09:46.399 --> 00:09:51.070
about the love of the game in 1989's Field
of Dreams, appeared alongside Richard Pryor

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:56.300
and Billy Dee Williams in 1976's The Bingo
Long Traveling All-Stars and Motor Kings,

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:00.600
and won a Tony Award in 1987 in August Wilson's
play Fences.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:06.639
Jones has also used his golden voice to narrate
on several occasions, including the 1984 documentary

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.780
There Was Always Sun Shining Someplace.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:13.230
Beyond his associations with baseball, the
distinguished, multi-award-winning actor has

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:18.050
been a fixture in film, TV, and onstage for
decades, though it is his booming baritone

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.680
voice that has become his most recognizable
talent.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:26.209
From Darth Vader to Mufasa Jones has become
the go-to guy for voices, narration, and commercials

00:10:26.209 --> 00:10:27.340
needing gravitas.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.800
"Totes mcgotes."

